\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces  Basic closed-loop control structure of the offset-free MPC. The observer receives the measured output $y$ and the applied input $u$ and delivers the lifted state estimate $\hat  {z}$ and the disturbance estimate $\hat  {d}$. The target optimization receives $\hat  {d}$ together with the setpoint $y_\text  {sp}$ and delivers the steady-state target $\bar  {y}$, and the MPC block receives $\bar  {y}$, $\hat  {z}$, and $\hat  {d}$ and delivers the input $u$ applied to the plant. \relax }}{6}{figure.caption.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:close_loop}{{3}{6}{Basic closed-loop control structure of the offset-free MPC. The observer receives the measured output $y$ and the applied input $u$ and delivers the lifted state estimate $\hat {z}$ and the disturbance estimate $\hat {d}$. The target optimization receives $\hat {d}$ together with the setpoint $y_\text {sp}$ and delivers the steady-state target $\bar {y}$, and the MPC block receives $\bar {y}$, $\hat {z}$, and $\hat {d}$ and delivers the input $u$ applied to the plant. \relax }{figure.caption.3}{}}
